# What never reaches the Docker daemon.
#
# This file is mostly a performance and correctness measure, and the two biggest
# entries are the reason it exists at all: `venv/` is ~6 GB and `results/` is
# ~1.5 GB of checkpoints and ONNX graphs. Without this, every `docker build`
# would upload all of it as build context before running a single instruction —
# and `results/` would then be *baked into* the image as well as mounted over it
# at runtime, which is a silent way to ship a stale checkpoint.

# Local environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Data and artifacts. Both arrive as volumes (see docker-compose.yml): the
# dataset read-only, the results directory read-write, so checkpoints and audit
# logs outlive the container.
data/
results/

# Secrets. The image must never contain a .env — the app reads <repo>/.env only
# as a fallback, and compose injects the real values as environment variables.
# A .env baked into a layer is a credential in a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Model artifacts, wherever they turn up
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.onnx

# Development-only material
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
Makefile
requirements-dev.txt
defect_detection_build_prompts.md

# The observability stack's own configuration is mounted into the prometheus and
# grafana containers, not copied into the API image.
docker/prometheus.yml
docker/grafana/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
